momentum sometimes thinking too much can  destroy your momentum Tom Watson my  condo is a total mess there are clothes  all over the living room floor my fridge  is almost empty today was the first time  I shaved in a week Evan what the heck  are you doing something big something  I'm excited about something that has  given me huge momentum I'm not making  things public yet but the teachable  lesson today is when you have momentum  stay in it for as long as possible  running the business is hard most of the  time you're just trying to keep up and  stay afloat that's why momentum is  important momentum is where the magic  happens when you've got momentum you're  getting things done quickly things that  might have taken you weeks do are flying  off your checklist you feel the energy  that it brings you you feel like your  business idea will work even though  everyone's telling you it won't if you  stop now you'll kill your momentum this  is where so many entrepreneurs make a  mistake you get a great idea something  that really excites you and you tell  yourself you'll do tomorrow or next week  and then you never do it if you're  excited by something take action right  away immediately send an email to  someone make a phone call visit a store  or library to do some research and do as  much as you can while you're in the zone  because that work will be gold for you  the work you do in one week when you're  feeling the momentum will be more  valuable than months of your usual work  push everything else meetings calls  emails and so on your usual daily  routine can wait this is too important  pay attention to it and don't let your  momentum slip away Evan this kind of  lifestyle isn't sustainable you're right  I'm a neat freak I hate clothes on the  floor I've got to eat I need some food  in the fridge at some point I'm gonna  need to get a great night's sleep again  this isn't sustainable for me or you  being in the zone isn't sustainable  either I don't know anyone who 